CM SYNTHESIZED 9-element Yagi matched to ZDA Communications ZDADJ433-12YG
CM (datasheet: 433 MHz Directional Antenna, item ZDADJ433-12YG).
CM
CM Extracted target specs from datasheet:
CM   Freq range      428-438 MHz (center 433.0 MHz used here)
CM   Gain            12 dBi
CM   Polarization    Horizontal/Vertical (mechanically adjustable - see
CM                   companion file *_vertical.nec, same rotation trick
CM                   used for PLC1669_9el_166MHz_vertical.nec)
CM   Beamwidth       45 deg (H-plane) / 35 deg (V-plane)
CM   VSWR            <= 1.5
CM   Front-to-Back   >= 15 dB
CM   Impedance       50 ohm, N-female, 200 W max
CM   Elements        9
CM   Boom length     1175 mm
CM
CM THIS IS NOT A REVERSE-ENGINEERED COPY - the datasheet does not publish
CM per-element lengths or spacing, only the aggregate specs above. Geometry
CM was DERIVED from the validated PLC1669_9el_166MHz.nec taper (real mfg
CM drawing) as follows:
CM   1. Frequency-scaled all 9 PLC1669 element lengths and spacings by
CM      166.380/433.000 (=0.384249), preserving the proven taper shape.
CM   2. Uniformly COMPRESSED spacing only (not lengths) by 0.93871x so
CM      total boom length lands exactly on the datasheet's 1175 mm spec.
CM      (PLC1669's own 9-element taper freq-scales to a slightly longer
CM      boom, 1.2517 m, than this product's 1.175 m - compressing spacing
CM      a bit is a normal design move, trades a little bandwidth for a
CM      tighter package, consistent with the tighter 45/35 deg beamwidths.)
CM Element count (9) matches the datasheet exactly, so no truncation of
CM PLC1669's director sequence was needed this time.
CM
CM CAVEAT: gain/beamwidth/F-B/VSWR against the targets above were NOT
CM verified by re-running NEC here. Expect the driven element length and
CM reflector spacing to need a few percent of retuning for zero feed
CM reactance once you run this through NEC2/4nec2/xnec2c.
CM
CM Element radius frequency-scaled from PLC1669's 3/8" OD stock to
CM 0.00183 m (~3.6 mm dia, ~1/8" rod) - swap for actual stock size.
CM Boom axis = X, elements along Y (HORIZONTAL polarization), height
CM Z = 6.0 m (change to match your mount). Feed = driven element (tag 2),
CM center segment. Ground = average (er=13, sigma=0.005 S/m) - swap GN
CM line for another terrain the same way as the other files in this set.
